<title>UK: UK court dismisses Camelot case.</title>
<headline>UK court dismisses Camelot case.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A UK court on Monday rejected am attempt by national lottery operator Camelot to have a numbers bet organised by UK bookmakers declared illegal.</p>
<p>Magistrate Ronald Bartle said he accepted the defence argument that the game was a bet and &quot;not a lottery&quot;  </p>
<p>49's is run by British bookmakers Coral, Ladbrokes and William Hill.</p>
<p>Punters bet on a sequence of numbers in a draw which is broadcast to betting shops up and down the country on their own television network.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
